@startuml client_connection_process_send_queue_activity
title ClientConnection - queued send dispatch

start
:ProcessSendQueueUnderLock(lock);
note right
    Entry: the caller holds send_mutex_ through lock.
    The procedure releases it around transport and callbacks,
    then reacquires it before changing queue or slot state.
end note

while (send_queue_ is non-empty?) is (yes)
    :Take the front command and remove it from send_queue_;
    if (command.callback is non-empty?) then (yes)
        :Move command.callback into waiting_for_reply_;
        :Unlock send_mutex_;
        :SendProtocolMessage(client_fd_, REQUEST, command.message);
        :Relock send_mutex_;
        :Return the command to the front of send_pool_;
        if (Transport succeeded?) then (yes)
            :Return with the reply slot engaged and lock held;
            stop
        else (no)
            :Move the reply callback out of waiting_for_reply_;
            :Keep the optional reply slot engaged;
            :Unlock send_mutex_;
            :Invoke the callback with the transport error;
            :Relock send_mutex_;
            :Reset waiting_for_reply_;
        endif
    else (no)
        :Set waiting_for_reply_ to an empty ReplyCallback marker;
        :Unlock send_mutex_;
        :SendProtocolMessage(client_fd_, SEND, command.message);
        :Ignore the transport result;
        :Relock send_mutex_;
        :Return the command to the front of send_pool_;
        :Reset waiting_for_reply_;
    endif
endwhile (no)

:Return with lock held;
stop

legend
    The queue is FIFO; recycled free commands are reused LIFO.
    A detached command stays reserved until transport finishes.
    A successful request releases its command storage before its reply.
    Its reply slot stays engaged and pauses remaining queue dispatch.
    Failed requests invoke their callback, then continue draining.
    The engaged slot also keeps reentrant requests queued during that callback.
    An empty callback selects SEND, not REQUEST, in this procedure.
    An empty queue at entry leaves the incoming reply-slot state unchanged.
    This is local dispatch control flow, not full send/stop reentrancy proof.
endlegend

@enduml